cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference the Palo Alto AI Research Lab community and AI-authorship policies, please cite them as below."
title: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab: default community health files and AI-authorship policy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/.github"
url: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - open source governance
  - AI authorship
  - contribution policy
  - community health files
abstract: >-
  The organisation-wide community documents inherited by every public repository of
  the lab — code of conduct, contributing, security and support policies — kept in
  one place rather than copied per repository, plus a lab-wide AI-authorship policy
  that credits a model on a commit only when its output changed that commit's
  content. Licenses are deliberately excluded, because GitHub does not inherit them.
  Presence of the required documents is enforced by a deterministic gate that runs
  outside the repositories it checks.
